<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean firms buy 50,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat.</title>
<headline>S.Korean firms buy 50,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean feed milling companies bought 50,000 tonnes of Canadian wheat at $145 a tonne C&amp;F, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>Japanese trading house Nissho Iwai Corp sold the wheat last week through private negotiations with shipment due June 5-25.</p>
<p>Arrival was set for by July 10 at the port of Inchon.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
